{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.MeasurementLimitedFloor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.MeasurementLimitedFloor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MeasurementFloor.qbeta_dashboard_err_ge_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MeasurementFloor.qbeta_dashboard_err_ge_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MeasurementLimitedFloor.lean#L70-L73","doc":"The Q_beta dashboard premise itself: the measured error exceeds one\nexperimental sigma (`779.7 <= 1248` ppb), so `miss_factor_ge_100` applies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MeasurementFloor.qbeta_dashboard_miss_ge_100","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MeasurementFloor.qbeta_dashboard_miss_ge_100","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MeasurementLimitedFloor.lean#L62-L68","doc":"**Concrete Q_beta instance** (2026-07-06/18 L2 dashboard values, in ppb):\n`sigma_exp = 779.7`, prediction error `1248`; the measured miss factor\n`1248 / (779.7/100) = 160.06...` is `>= 100`. Pure `norm_num` — records the\ndashboard arithmetic as a checked fact, not a new measurement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MeasurementFloor.err_lt_sigma_of_beats_target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MeasurementFloor.err_lt_sigma_of_beats_target","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MeasurementLimitedFloor.lean#L54-L60","doc":"Contrapositive, the actionable reading: beating the 100x target forces the\nprediction error strictly below one experimental sigma — i.e. below the\nmeasurement floor. Absent a substrate-q_0 derivation, the anchor-dependence\ntheorems exclude exactly this for the c_3-routed observables. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MeasurementFloor.hundredfold_target_unreachable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MeasurementFloor.hundredfold_target_unreachable","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MeasurementLimitedFloor.lean#L48-L52","doc":"The 100x target itself is strictly unreachable under the same premise:\n`sigma/100 < err` whenever `0 < sigma <= err`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MeasurementFloor.miss_factor_ge_100","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MeasurementFloor.miss_factor_ge_100","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MeasurementLimitedFloor.lean#L37-L46","doc":"**Gate arithmetic.** If a prediction's error is at least one experimental\nsigma (`sigma <= err`), the miss factor against the 100x target `sigma/100`\nis at least `100`. This is the arithmetic backbone of the measurement-limited\nceiling: the anchor-dependence theorems supply `sigma <= err` for the\nc_3-routed observables; this lemma converts it into the L2-dashboard\nstatement \"misses 100x by >= 100x\". ","signatureChunk":0}]}